'\"
.TH "rbc::LEGEND" 3tcl 0\&.5\&.0 "rbc" "Upgraded Tcl/Tk9\&.0-ready RBC package"
.SH NAME
rbc::LEGEND - Commands in namespace rbc::LEGEND
.SH "GRAPH LEGEND LEGEND COMMAND"
.PP
Commands in this namespace document the graph legend\&.
.PP
LEGEND is used below as a placeholder for:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
GRAPHINST legend
.fi
.RE
.PP
The legend displays an entry for graph elements\&. Each entry contains the element's symbol and label and uses the
drawing attributes of that element\&.
.PP
For example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
graph \&.g

\&.g element create signal1 -x {0 1 2 3} -y {1 4 2 5} -label "Input"
\&.g element create signal2 -x {0 1 2 3} -y {3 2 5 4} -label "Output"
\&.g legend configure -position rightmargin
.fi
.RE
.PP
The legend is a single component of the graph\&. Unlike elements, markers, or pens, there are no named legend
objects\&.
.SH "LEGEND ENTRIES"
.PP
Legend entries correspond to graph elements\&. The element's -label option supplies the text displayed in the
legend\&.
.PP
The order of legend entries follows the element display order\&.
.PP
Legend entries may be made active independently of the corresponding graph elements:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g legend activate signal1
\&.g legend deactivate signal1
.fi
.RE
.PP
Activating a legend entry changes only the appearance of the entry in the legend\&. It does not activate the
corresponding data points or change how the element is drawn in the plotting area\&.
.PP
To activate both independently:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g legend activate signal1
\&.g element activate signal1
.fi
.RE
.SH "LEGEND POSITION"
.PP
The -position option determines where the legend is displayed\&.
.TS
tab(|) box;
l l.
Position| Description
_
leftmargin| Draws the legend in the left graph margin\&.
rightmargin| Draws the legend in the right graph margin\&. This is the default\&.
topmargin| Draws the legend in the top graph margin\&.
bottommargin | Draws the legend in the bottom graph margin\&.
plotarea| Draws the legend inside the plotting area\&.
@x,y| Places the legend at the specified screen coordinates\&.
\&.window| Creates an external legend window with the specified Tk pathname\&.
.TE
.PP
For example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g legend configure -position plotarea -anchor ne
.fi
.RE
.PP
places the legend in the upper-right part of the plotting area\&.
.PP
An explicit screen position may also be used:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g legend configure -position @20,30 -anchor nw
.fi
.RE
.PP
For an @x,y position, negative coordinates are measured from the opposite edge of the graph\&. For example, a
negative X coordinate is relative to the right edge and a negative Y coordinate is relative to the bottom edge\&.
.PP
A pathname beginning with \&. selects an external legend window:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g legend configure -position \&.legend
.fi
.RE
.PP
Rbc creates the window at that pathname and draws the legend into it\&. If the external legend window is
destroyed, the legend returns to rightmargin\&.
.PP
The -anchor option controls how the legend is positioned relative to its selected site or screen coordinate\&.
.SH "LEGEND LAYOUT"
.PP
Legend entries are arranged as a table\&.
.PP
-rows and -columns can be used to request a particular table shape:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g legend configure -columns 2
.fi
.RE
.PP
A value of 0 leaves that dimension automatic\&.
.PP
-ipadx and -ipady specify padding inside individual legend entries\&. -padx and -pady specify padding
around the outside of the complete legend\&.
.PP
Each padding value may contain either one screen distance or two:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g legend configure -ipadx {2 6} -pady {4 8}
.fi
.RE
.PP
A single value applies equally to both sides\&. Two values specify the two sides independently\&.
.SH "ACTIVE ENTRIES"
.PP
LEGEND activate marks entries for drawing with the active legend style and returns the names of all entries
that are currently active\&.
.PP
The active appearance is controlled by:
.TP
\(bu
-activebackground
.TP
\(bu
-activeborderwidth
.TP
\(bu
-activeforeground
.TP
\(bu
-activerelief
.PP
For example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g legend configure -activebackground lightblue -activeforeground navy -activerelief raised
\&.g legend activate signal1
.fi
.RE
.PP
LEGEND deactivate restores the normal legend appearance\&.
.SH "LEGEND BINDINGS"
.PP
Event bindings may be associated with legend entries using LEGEND bind\&.
.PP
Element names act as binding tags for their corresponding legend entries:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g legend bind signal1 <Button-1> {
    puts "signal1"
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
The element under the current pointer may be obtained with LEGEND get and used by a binding:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g legend bind all <Button-1> {
    set element [\&.g legend get current]
    puts $element
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
LEGEND get can also identify the entry at an explicit screen position\&.
.SH "LEGEND OPTIONS"
.TS
tab(|) box;
l l.
Option| Description
_
-activebackground color| Specifies the background color used for active legend entries\&.
-activeborderwidth distance | Specifies the border width around an active legend entry\&. The default is 2\&.
-activeforeground color| Specifies the text color used for active legend entries\&.
-activerelief relief| Specifies the relief used for active legend entries\&. The default is flat\&.
-anchor anchor| Specifies how the legend is positioned relative to the location selected by -position\&. The default is n\&.
-background color| Specifies the legend background\&. An empty value makes the legend background transparent\&.
-bg color| Synonym for -background\&.
-borderwidth distance| Specifies the width of the border around the complete legend\&.
-bd distance| Synonym for -borderwidth\&.
-columns number| Requests the number of columns used to arrange legend entries\&. 0 selects automatic layout\&. The default is 0\&.
-font font| Specifies the font used for element labels in the legend\&.
-foreground color| Specifies the normal text color of legend entries\&.
-fg color| Synonym for -foreground\&.
-hide boolean| Specifies whether the legend is hidden\&. The default is no\&.
-ipadx padding| Specifies horizontal padding inside each legend entry\&. The default is 1\&.
-ipady padding| Specifies vertical padding inside each legend entry\&. The default is 1\&.
-padx padding| Specifies horizontal padding around the complete legend\&. The default is 1\&.
-pady padding| Specifies vertical padding around the complete legend\&. The default is 1\&.
-position position| Specifies where the legend is drawn\&. Accepted forms are leftmargin, rightmargin, topmargin, bottommargin, plotarea, \&.window, and @x,y\&. The default is rightmargin\&.
-raised boolean| Specifies whether the legend is drawn above graph elements when the legend overlaps the plotting area\&. The default is no\&.
-relief relief| Specifies the relief of the border around the complete legend\&. The default is sunken\&.
-rows number| Requests the number of rows used to arrange legend entries\&. 0 selects automatic layout\&. The default is 0\&.
-shadow shadow| Specifies a shadow for legend entry text\&. An empty value disables the shadow\&.
.TE
.PP
Legend configuration options may also be set through Tk's option database\&. The resource name is legend and
the resource class is Legend\&.
.PP
For example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
option add *Graph\&.legend\&.Foreground navy
option add *Graph\&.Legend\&.Relief raised
.fi
.RE

